  "live_records": {
    "q-72744": {
      "dom_id": "step-q72744",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Suppose $X$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $det(X)=-3.$ What is the value of $det(7X)?$",
      "worked_solution": "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot X)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(X).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=7$ and $n=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(7X) & ={7}^{2}\\cdot det(X) \\\\  & =49\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-147.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
